WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.660
Let's build a website for Willow and Coast
Wellness.

2
00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:06.740
Then follow the customer experience from
the first preview into the customer

3
00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:11.600
portal. We'll choose a design, make it our
own, add a custom photo and explore

4
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:15.760
publishing and inquiries. This
demonstration uses a test business and a

5
00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:20.660
test checkout. Start with the business
details, the name, what you offer and the

6
00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:22.760
contact information you want people to
see.

7
00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:26.500
Use an email address you control for
checkout and website access.

8
00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:31.740
Keep the description specific. A few clear
sentences help you see how the design will

9
00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:33.880
introduce the business to potential
clients.

10
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:37.360
Next, choose the mood and style that fit
the business.

11
00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:40.360
The matching step brings up template
options to explore.

12
00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:44.520
Open a design, look at its layout, and
compare another if you need to.

13
00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:48.960
Choose a starting point you like, then use
the preview to see where your own content

14
00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:52.620
belongs. Now make the preview sound like
Willow and Coast.

15
00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:56.980
Double-click an editable text area,
replace the headline, and check how it

16
00:00:56.980 --> 00:01:00.660
sits in the design. Explore the available
colors and fonts, too.

17
00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:05.380
Keep the wording clear and the page easy
to scan so visitors can quickly understand

18
00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:09.800
what the business offers. The selected
design and business details carry into the

19
00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:14.200
order. Review the plan, price, and terms,
then continue to stripe.

20
00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:17.740
This demonstration uses a test checkout
with no real charge.

21
00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:21.740
After checkout completes, the website is
provisioned and the portal shows

22
00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:24.580
published. Now we can start managing the
site.

23
00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.120
The delivery email includes a private link
to the customer portal.

24
00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:31.500
Open that link to manage your website and
keep it somewhere safe.

25
00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:36.160
The portal brings together your business
details, website status, images, and

26
00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:39.960
inquiries. It's the place to return
whenever you want to update something or

27
00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:44.400
check a new message. Inside the portal,
let's update Willow and Coast's tagline

28
00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:46.340
and choose Save and Publish.

29
00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:50.660
The update completes successfully and the
new wording appears on the hosted website.

30
00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:54.200
The portal also provides the supported
business and service fields.

31
00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:58.520
Review your changes carefully, publish
them, and check the page your visitors

32
00:01:58.520 --> 00:01:59.180
will see.

33
00:01:59.333 --> 00:02:04.273
Now let's add a custom photo. In the
portal, open Images and choose Upload.

34
00:02:04.273 --> 00:02:07.853
Select your photo from your computer and
wait for its thumbnail to appear.

35
00:02:08.093 --> 00:02:11.953
The image library keeps website-ready
images available for this site.

36
00:02:12.073 --> 00:02:16.593
Use clear, well-lit photos that represent
your business and keep each source file

37
00:02:16.593 --> 00:02:21.153
under four megabytes. To put the photo
into the design, open the visual editor

38
00:02:21.153 --> 00:02:25.513
and continue to the preview. Click the
image you want to replace, then choose the

39
00:02:25.513 --> 00:02:29.593
photo from your computer. Here, our
coaching room photo replaces the original

40
00:02:29.593 --> 00:02:33.453
picture. Check its crop and the
surrounding text so the section still

41
00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:35.333
feels balanced and easy to read.

42
00:02:35.473 --> 00:02:39.093
Finally, choose Publish to Live Site and
wait for the confirmation.

43
00:02:39.353 --> 00:02:42.153
Then, open the actual website and refresh
it.

44
00:02:42.233 --> 00:02:46.353
There is the new photo, alongside the
updated business wording and headline.

45
00:02:46.513 --> 00:02:48.773
This final check closes the loop.

46
00:02:48.833 --> 00:02:52.933
The changes are visible to visitors, and
you can return to the portal whenever your

47
00:02:52.933 --> 00:02:54.313
content needs another update.

48
00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:57.060
Let's test what happens when a visitor
gets in touch.

49
00:02:57.180 --> 00:03:00.680
On the published website, Jordan sends a
sample enquiry.

50
00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:04.700
Back in the portal, the message appears
with the sender's details and the

51
00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:08.800
notification status. The email
notification also arrived in our inbox.

52
00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:12.060
To respond, use Reply in your email app.

53
00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:15.800
Your saved enquiry stays available here,
so you can keep track of the

54
00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:19.840
conversation's starting point. Your
account dashboard brings the website and

55
00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:24.160
its management tools together. Manage
Billing opens Stripe, where you can review

56
00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:26.780
the subscription, payment method, and
invoices.

57
00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:29.540
The website already has a hosted address.

58
00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:32.900
If you own a domain, the portal provides
connection instructions.

59
00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:38.160
Website records, image storage, and email
notifications are managed for you.

60
00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:40.140
From here, the routine is simple.

61
00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:44.960
Update your content, publish, check the
live result, and respond to enquiries.

